{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"S5 (5851): CI patchset 2 revealed an ORDERING-dependent failure masked by my local xdist run — 6 review-bot tests failed serially because app.state.startup_binding is set at import, so lifespan always called _worker(queue,cfg,runtime) 3-arg, breaking tests that monkeypatch _worker with a 2-arg stub. Root-cause fix: lifespan always calls _worker(queue,cfg) 2-arg; _worker resolves runtime from app.state.startup_binding internally. Validated SERIALLY: 270 passed across full blast radius (review_bot/snapshot/complexity). NOTE: full serial suite is ~2hr on this machine; relying on CI serial matrix as the authoritative gate. Amended 0e417bff05, pushed patchset 3."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787075357225276001,"uuid":"4cd83e3a-e7e9-4d5e-9da1-45471d9226d9"}